infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title The one shift that changes everything
  desc From a static document to a living UI that is a function of state
  compares
    - label Web page
      children
        - label Mostly static
          desc HTML arrives, a little JS runs, done
        - label DOM touched by hand
          desc Code reaches in and mutates elements directly
        - label No shared state model
          desc Each script tracks its own bits, ad hoc
        - label Cracks as it grows
          desc One change quietly breaks an unrelated part
    - label Application
      children
        - label Living UI
          desc Holds data that changes, re-draws in response
        - label UI = f(state)
          desc State changes, the framework re-renders for you
        - label One-directional data flow
          desc Props down, state owned locally, predictable
        - label Scales across a team
          desc Twenty people ship features without firefighting
theme
  palette #f59e0b #14b8a6
